{"id": "EUVD-2026-97007", "enisaUuid": "bdd1212e-2c64-30ba-b641-fb560dfe0993", "description": "UnicomAI Wanwu through 0.6.5 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows authenticated users to mint AppKeys bound to other users' MCP servers via POST /v1/appspace/app/key. Attackers supplying a victim's MCP server UUID with appType mcpserver can open MCP sessions and invoke the server's tools using the victim's upstream authentication.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T13:26:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:41:14", "baseScore": 2.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/unicomai-wanwu-mcp-key-arbitrary-resource", "https://github.com/UnicomAI/wanwu/blob/v0.6.5/internal/app-service/client/orm/app_key.go#L37-L49", "https://github.com/UnicomAI/wanwu/blob/v0.6.5/internal/bff-service/server/http/middleware/auth_openapi.go#L46-L70", "https://github.com/UnicomAI/wanwu", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/unicomai-wanwu-through-0.6.5-authorization-bypass-via-v1-appspace-app-key-appkey-minting"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108856", "GHSA-5pv8-92g5-57vm"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8d05f923-43bb-3046-a1c6-4f1dafdbcd75", "product": {"name": "Wanwu", "vendor": {"name": "UnicomAI"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.6.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "56a11d51-73ec-340b-823a-4236f9f5b3f1", "vendor": {"name": "UnicomAI"}}], "isExploited": false}